---
page article
---
{# A rich-text page. Three things worth reading closely:

   1. `<title>` is RCDATA. Interpolation is allowed there and is escaped with
      the RCDATA rules, but an Html value can never render inside it (O2075).
   2. `<json-ld>` takes exactly one record expression and is serialized by the
      engine — strings are emitted with `<`, `>`, `&` and `/` escaped as \uXXXX,
      so the payload can never close the script element it lives in.
   3. `richtext` is a HOST filter declared `unsafeHtml: true`. Its return type
      is Html, the engine's terminal type: it renders unescaped, only in
      element content, and every call site raises the O2071 warning. The host
      owns the sanitizer; the engine only owns the fact that you were told. #}
<title>{article.title} - {shopName}</title>

<main class="article" id="main">
  <json-ld>{{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Article",
    headline: article.title,
    datePublished: article.publishedAt,
    url: article.url,
    author: {
      "@type": "Person",
      name: article.author.name
    }
  }}</json-ld>

  <header class="article__header">
    <h1 class="article__title">{article.title}</h1>

    <p class="article__byline">
      <if {article.author.avatar != none}>
        <img
          class="article__avatar"
          src={imgUrl(article.author.avatar, 96)}
          alt={article.author.name}
          width="96"
          height="96"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </if>

      <if {article.author.url != none}>
        <a class="article__author" href={article.author.url} rel="author">{article.author.name}</a>
      </if>
      <else>
        <span class="article__author">{article.author.name}</span>
      </else>

      <time class="article__date" datetime={article.publishedAt}>
        {article.publishedAt |> formatDate("MMMM D, YYYY")}
      </time>
    </p>

    <if {size(article.tags) > 0}>
      <ul class="article__tags">
        <for tag of={article.tags} limit={8}>
          <li class="article__tag"><a href="/blog/tagged/{tag |> slugify}">{tag}</a></li>
        </for>
      </ul>
    </if>
  </header>

  <div class="article__body">
    {article.bodyHtml |> richtext}
  </div>

  <footer class="article__footer">
    <p class="article__summary">{article.excerpt ?? "Thanks for reading."}</p>
  </footer>
</main>
